IV. EXPERIMENTS
We evaluate SuperFusion for the long-range HD map generation task on nuScenes [2] and a self-collected dataset.
A. Implementation Details
Model. We use ResNet-101 [13] as our camera branch backbone and PointPillars [16] as our LiDAR branch backbone. For depth estimation, we modify DeepLabV3 [4] to generate pixel-wise probability distribution of depth bins. The camera backbone is initialized using the DeepLabV3 [4] semantic segmentation model pre-trained on the MS-COCO dataset [22]. All other components are randomly initialized. We set the image size to 256 × 704 and voxelize the LiDAR point cloud with 0.15 m resolution. We use [0, 90] m × [−15, 15] m as the range of the BEV HD maps, which results in a size of 600 × 200. We set the discretized depth bins to 2.0 – 90.0 m spaced by 1.0 m. Training Details. We train the model for 30 epochs using stochastic gradient descent with a learning rate of 0.1. For the instance embedding, we set α = β = 1, δd = 3.0, and δv = 0.5. We set λdep = 1.0, λseg = 1.0, λins = 1.0, and λdir = 0.2 for different weighting factors.
